# Deploy

**Published** on https://rtikhonov.com is the Lovable app. This Worker
does not own `rtikhonov.com` or `www`. Those names are DNS-only CNAMEs
to `pixel-perfect-capture-3633.lovable.app`. Do not attach them as
Worker custom domains, and do not proxy them (orange cloud returns
error 1014). When asked what is live, check the URL.

**CI/CD is Cloudflare Workers Builds.** Merge to `main` deploys Worker
`rtikhonov` without those hostnames. GitHub is version control only.
Never add GitHub Pages, `.github/workflows/`, `actions/deploy-pages`,
`withastro/action`, or `cloudflare/wrangler-action`.

The Astro app is the **repository root** (`wrangler.jsonc` here). There is
no second Astro tree and no `cursor/cloudflare-workers-hosting` branch to
fetch.

## Ship

1. Large change (new page or new UI): look first — skill `preview-site`.
   Small change (typo, blog note, tiny copy): skip that.
2. `npm run check` if the tree is dirty.
3. Merge the PR to `main`.
4. Confirm the Worker on its `*.workers.dev` URL. The public domain
   stays on Lovable.

Setup or pipeline questions → skill `workers-builds-ci`.
Dashboard settings → `docs/deploy.md`.

## Emergency only

`npm run deploy` (Wrangler) is for a Builds outage, never a CI test. It
needs `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` with **Workers Scripts Edit**; `whoami` can
pass while deploy returns 403. Never wait on a `wrangler login` localhost
callback in Cloud.

## Do not

- Offer two ship paths, or ask which setup to use. This is the path.
- TodoWrite, `git diff main...HEAD`, or re-run `check:docs` for a
  clean-tree ship.
- Add `test.rtikhonov.com` unless the owner asks for it as its own task.
